Here are the corrections and tips for the student's sentences:

**Sentence:** Hi my name is and I'm glad to be able to meet you.
**Correction:** Hi, my name is [Your Name], and I'm glad to be able to meet you.
**Tip:**  Always include a greeting and introduce yourself clearly.  

**Sentence:** So I'm really excited because with your help I will improve my English.
**Correction:** So, I'm really excited because with your help, I will improve my English.
**Tip:**  Use "because" to connect the two clauses and "I will improve" is a more natural way to express your goal.

**Sentence:** So, I would say that my principal focus is improve my speaking.
**Correction:** So, I would say that my principal focus is improving my speaking.
**Tip:**  Use "improving" instead of "improve" for the verb.  "Principal focus" can be replaced with "main focus" or "primary goal".

**Sentence:** I implemented this application when I talk with you, call it free speak.
**Correction:** I implemented this application when I talk with you; it's called FreeSpeak.
**Tip:**  Use a semicolon to separate the independent clauses.  The word "it" is used to refer to the application. 


Remember, practice makes perfect! Keep working on your English, and you'll continue to improve.

